id=a52sxq_devicestate
name=Galaxy A52s 5G non-foldable device state
author=CodesRahul96
description=The source services.jar hardcodes Samsung's foldable device-state machine: DeviceStateManagerService always builds FlexibleDeviceStatePolicy/Provider with the six fold states and the AOSP default provider was stripped. Without a folding sensor the provider settles on CLOSED, whose properties make WindowManager, CameraServiceProxy, AOD and apps treat the phone as a folded foldable. Hand the provider a single property-less DEFAULT state instead, like AOSP does on non-foldables, but with identifier 3 rather than AOSP's 0: Samsung's fold code compares raw identifiers and 0 is CLOSED on the Fold. Only applies to foldable sources (SEC_FLOATING_FEATURE_FRAMEWORK_SUPPORT_FOLDABLE_TYPE_FOLD, the Fold8 base it was written for); a no-op on flat sources such as the S25 and the current S26 Ultra base.
